+Current-source time and receipt time are independent:
+
+| Clock | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| Model `currentTime`, `currentZone`, `currentValidAt` | Raw current-model wall-time text, the captured request zone, and the derived valid epoch in that zone; retrieval never replaces this source clock. |
+| Model `currentIntervalSec` | The positive preceding interval ending at `currentValidAt`; it is a duration, not an epoch or instantaneous-rate label. |
+| Model `retrievedAt` | Client wall-clock receipt after fetch/body consumption, preserved when reloading the weather cache. |
+| Radar `frameGeneratedAt` | The selected mosaic frame's numeric seconds converted to a finite millisecond epoch; not each contributing radar's local observation time. |
+| Radar `indexGeneratedAt` | The separate manifest/index generation epoch; it cannot replace missing frame time or renew an old frame. |
+| Radar `retrievedAt` | Client wall-clock receipt after Image consumption, separate from both generation clocks. |
+
+Provider processing duration is not an epoch and does not renew freshness. In
+ordinary real time, both model source and receipt ages must be nonfuture and at
+most 900,000 ms (15 minutes), inclusively, with a positive current interval and
+matching target generation. Admission may retain an ineligible record for
+diagnostics; selection withdraws its current condition, temperature, cloud
+drivers and particles. A valid hourly track does not renew current time.
+RainViewer frame age and receipt age are each nonfuture and at most 1,200,000 ms,
+inclusively. Index time cannot substitute for missing frame time. Numeric frame
+and index seconds, and their converted millisecond epochs, must be finite before
+Image dispatch or metadata installation. Finite metadata is not local coverage,
+an observation or a precipitation amount. Future tolerance is zero for those
+source and receipt clocks.
+
+Weather cache loading accepts only `0 <= now - receipt < 6 hours`; exactly six
+hours is a cache miss. This is a read/admission window, not six hours of current
+authority or an automatic deletion promise. Cache misses preserve stored bytes;
+loading keeps the original receipt and cannot renew the current source clock.
+When the ordinary unavailable state is painted, the
+header shows an em dash, temperature is blank and unsupported weather effects
+are off. The date-keyed prayer cache has its own admission/recovery rules; weather
+retention does not describe prayer-cache validity or guarantee offline service.
+Source/receipt/cache ages rely on the client's wall clock: an incorrect clock or
+skew can reject recent evidence or misclassify freshness. No clock correction,
+local observation, universal coverage or guaranteed offline availability follows.
+
+Current model precipitation is an amount for the preceding declared interval,
+not an instantaneous rate. Any reported mm/h conversion is labelled an interval
+average; an unrepresentable derived value stays unavailable. Missing or invalid
+quantities remain null. A numerical zero is preserved and supplies no wet effect.
+Synthetic point rates and interval amounts retain their units and measurement
+windows. An unavailable probability is not zero: the optional owned QA forecast
+producer accepts zero only with an explicit precipitation event and matching
+future interval. Production hourly probability/event fields remain unavailable.
+
+The current `preceding-interval-amount` covers `currentValidAt` minus
+`currentIntervalSec * 1000` through `currentValidAt` (epoch milliseconds); an mm/h
+conversion is an interval average, not an instantaneous rate. The hourly
+`preceding-hour-amount` belongs to the selected forecast interval from `validFrom`
+to `validUntil`, never to live-current observation. The production hourly
+projection retains null `issuedAt`, `probability` and `probabilityEvent`, and
+reports `native/interpolated provenance unavailable` for resolution.
+
+Unavailable temperature paints blank; an admitted temperature of zero paints
+`0°`, with the existing integer rounding. Finite negative Celsius/Fahrenheit
+temperatures are valid. Units belong to the captured request; supplied conflicting
+unit metadata is rejected, while absent optional metadata uses that request's
+units. A valid, otherwise eligible condition can remain visible when optional
+temperature or other measurements are absent. Normalization retains null plus
+`unavailable` or `invalid measurement` reasons rather than manufacturing zero.
+Missing/invalid precipitation cannot independently authorize wet particles; a
+genuine zero is a dry model amount, not a direct local measurement. This prose
+introduces no validator dependency, cache schema change or migration, and cannot
+retroactively distinguish an older coerced zero from a genuine measurement.
+
+One admitted decision supplies `weatherInformation(decision, day)`. Its cached
+`currentText`, `spatialText`, `horizonText` and `forecastText` are combined into
+the weather title and clipped, non-hidden `#weather-information` description.
+The icon's accessible name stays concise; the detailed summary appears once in
+its description. In local mode the existing Widget settings button references
+that description while retaining its action name, persistence warning, role,
+tab order and focus behaviour. Absolute approach/forecast intervals use the
+configured target time zone. Current wet evidence and a later approach remain
+independent. Nearby precipitation without a qualified trajectory has no arrival
+interval. Missing, ineligible and unsupported information is explicit. Formatting
+does not fetch, admit evidence, change WMO/temperature or grant effect permissions.
+
+Present/nearby/approach positives are owned, explicit SIM fixtures, not live
+observation adapters. The optional forecast dependency decorator is test-only
+and refuses ordinary live installation. No useful arrival service, calibrated
+probability, radar-derived millimetres or arrival-accuracy claim is supported.
+
+The `synthetic-present-v1` present/nearby contract is exclusive to the explicit
+simulation-fixture lane. It requires the Synthetic QA provider/product, matching
+target generation, underlying source/receipt/validity times, qualified coverage
+and operational health. A `trusted:true` field, radar image or forecast does not
+admit this lane. Expiry, an outage or missing evidence withdraws its unsupported
+present permissions; independently eligible current-model visualPermissions
+retain their own quantitative policy.
+
